{"name":"Loose cotton clothing / washing sheets","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":0,"casual":{"lead":["Some people wear loose cotton and wash sheets often to reduce acne from rubbing and trapped sweat.","General references suggest loose breathable fabric for acne mechanica; no trials were found."],"sections":[{"h":"How it works","paras":["Looser, breathable fabric reduces friction, heat and sweat retention on skin."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks and caveats","paras":["No harms are described."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[],"links":{"studies":[],"trials":[],"label":null,"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Squat 6 [O] Bench 4 [X] and Be Leaner [ / ]","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/squat-6-o-bench-4-x-and-be-leaner/223615","site":"T Nation · 632 posts · 2016"},{"title":"My Own 'Clinic'","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/my-own-clinic/95705","site":"T Nation · 196 posts · 2007"},{"title":"TRT Effects on Skin","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/trt-effects-on-skin/227035","site":"T Nation · 113 posts · 2017"},{"title":"Help - Bacne","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/help-bacne/140390","site":"T Nation · 22 posts · 2009"},{"title":"Bacne?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/bacne/50930","site":"T Nation · 17 posts · 2005"},{"title":"Vitamins & Acne","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/vitamins-acne/151987","site":"T Nation · 9 posts · 2010"}],"web":[{"title":"Acne mechanica - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acne_mechanica"},{"title":"Folliculitis - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Folliculitis"}]},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Wearing loose, breathable clothing such as cotton and washing bedding regularly are habits adopted to reduce friction- and occlusion-related acne.[1]","Wikipedia says acne mechanica arises from friction, heat and pressure, and suggests loose-fitting, breathable fabrics such as cotton over synthetics; the page is flagged as needing more reliable medical sources.[1] It also lists clothing friction as a trigger of folliculitis.[2]"],"infobox":